WEBVTT

00:34:58.176 --> 00:35:01.406
And at "National Review" in the old days,
we had a sort of a tension

00:35:01.430 --> 00:35:04.164
between the real Milton Friedman
free-market conservatives

00:35:04.188 --> 00:35:05.585
and the social conservatives.

00:35:05.609 --> 00:35:08.888
But by the time Reagan came along
and let alone Paul Ryan,

00:35:08.912 --> 00:35:11.099
the individualists had won.

00:35:11.123 --> 00:35:13.708
And so it became
all-corporate free market.

00:35:13.732 --> 00:35:16.163
And the idea that there was
any social cohesion

00:35:16.187 --> 00:35:18.423
that was being ripped apart
by the free market,

00:35:18.447 --> 00:35:21.030
that all was given lip service
but no real message.

00:35:21.054 --> 00:35:24.330
And conservatism drifted off
into this hyperindividualism,

00:35:24.354 --> 00:35:26.382
which has left us, in part, where we were.

00:35:26.406 --> 00:35:31.449
Free-market economics doesn't give you
a way to moralize the market.